We found the mean number of off-road glances longer than 2 seconds of M = 1.09 ( SD = 1.54) for the Baseline and M = 0.74 ( SD = 0.96) for the ARHUD. Due to the violation of the normality distribution, we conducted a Mann-Whitney test showing no significant difference between the Baseline and ARHUD ( U = 234.5, p = 0.657).
C. Subjective Data

The usability score ( Fig. 7 ) had a mean of M = 66.04 ( SD = 16.12) for the Baseline and a mean of M = 73.85 ( SD = 14.01) for the ARHUD. An independent t-test revealed a significantly higher usability for the ARHUD ( t (46) = −1.792, p = 0.040, d = 0.517, one-tailed). The trust in automation score ( Fig. 7 ) revealed a significantly higher trust ( t (46) = 1.876, p = 0.033, d = 0.542, one-tailed) for the ARHUD M = 3.00 ( SD = 0.51) compared to the Baseline M = 2.70 ( SD = 0.58). An exploratory analysis of trust scores in the ARHUD condition showed no reduction in trust with no crash ( M = 2.84, SD = 0.41, n = 11) compared to one crash ( M = 3.15, SD = 0.59, n = 11) and two crashes ( M = 3.08, SD = 0.56, n = 2) at a descriptive level. The acceptance rating ( Fig. 7 ) consisted of the usefulness and satisfaction score. The participants reported no significantly higher satisfaction ( t (46) = −1.942, p = 0.029, α H o l m = 0.025, one-tailed) for the ARHUD ( M = 0.93, SD = 0.69) compared to the Baseline ( M = 0.50, SD = 0.82). Due to the violation of the normality assumption, a conducted Mann-Whitney test ( U = 237.5, p = 0.150, α H o l m = 0.05, one-tailed) revealed no higher usefulness rating for the ARHUD ( M = 0.89, SD = 0.61) than for the Baseline ( M = 0.56, SD = 0.90). Table VI displays the means and standard deviations of the subjective workload for the longitudinal and lateral malfunction. The conducted ANOVA for the subjective workload showed neither a significant effect for the HMI concept ( F (1,46) = 2.252, p = 0.140), nor for the malfunction scenario ( F (1,46) = 2.498, p = 0.121) or the interaction effect between the HMI concept and scenario ( F (1,46) = 0.039, p = 0.845).
